questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput ledger service experiences silent data loss and missing database rollbacks. You inspect the following Spring service implementation:

java
@Service
public class AccountTransferService {
    private final Map<String, BigDecimal> balanceCache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public void executeBatch(List<TransferRequest> requests) {
        for (TransferRequest req : requests) {
            this.applyTransfer(req.getAccountId(), req.getAmount());
        }
    }

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void applyTransfer(String accountId, BigDecimal delta) {
        BigDecimal current = balanceCache.getOrDefault(accountId, BigDecimal.ZERO);
        balanceCache.put(accountId, current.add(delta));
        persistToDatabase(accountId, delta);
    }

    private void persistToDatabase(String accountId, BigDecimal delta) {
        // JDBC/JPA persist operations
    }
}


Under high concurrency, metric monitors show that the transactional rollback handlers configured on `applyTransfer` are never executed during database write failures, and concurrent updates to the same `accountId` produce stale balance values.
